==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|wīt}}, {{IPA|en|/waɪt/}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪt|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|wight}}; {{a|in accents with the [[wine-whine merger]]}} [[white]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|wīten||to accuse, reproach, punish, suspect}}, {{inh|en|ang|wītan||to look, behold, see, guard, keep, impute or ascribe to, accuse, reproach, blame}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wītan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wītaną}}. Connected to Old English {{m|ang|wīte}}, see below.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|wyte}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}} {{term-label|en|transitive|archaic|or|obsolete}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|Scotland}} To [[regard#Verb|regard]] (someone) as [[guilty]], to [[accuse]], to [[blame#Verb|blame]], to [[fault#Verb|fault]].
# To [[censure#Verb|censure]] (someone); to [[mulct#Verb|mulct]], to [[reproach#Verb|reproach]].
#* {{RQ:Spenser Colin Clout|sig=D3|verso=1|page=28|passage=[U]niuſtly thou doeſt '''vvyte''' them all, / For that vvhich thou miſlikedſt in a fevv.}}
# To [[guard#Verb|guard]] (something); to [[keep#Verb|keep]], to [[observe]], [[preserve#Verb|preserve]], [[protect]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|wite|t=guilt, blameworthiness, blame, wrongdoing, misdeed, offense, punishment, retribution, fine, bote, customary rent}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wīte|t=punishment, pain, torment}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wītī}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wītiją}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weyd-|t=to see, find, behold}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|outside|Scotland}} [[blame|Blame]], [[responsibility]], [[guilt]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1922|author={{w|Eric Rücker Eddison|E. R. Eddison}}|title=[http://gutenberg.net.au/ebooks06/0602051.txt The Worm Ouroboros]
|publisher={{w|Project Gutenberg Australia|The Project Gutenberg, Australia}}
|passage=Nor I will not suffer mine indignation so to [[witwanton]] with fair justice as persuade me to put the '''wite''' on Witchland.}}
# [[punishment|Punishment]], [[penalty]], [[fine]], [[bote]], [[mulct]].

===Etymology 3===
From {{inh|en|enm|witen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wītan|t=to see, accuse, go, depart}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*wītan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*wītaną}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*weyd-|t=to see, find, behold}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|or|poetic}} To [[go]], go away, [[depart]], [[perish]], [[vanish]]

